#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""deskmap: read and control the running Deskmap app (macOS window/desktop router).

Deskmap keeps windows on fixed desktops and screens through RULES: app (+ optional
title fragments) -> screen/desktop/layout, separately for two MODES: "docked"
(external monitor connected) and "undocked" (laptop only). Rules live in PROFILES;
one profile is active. A rule's layout is applied once per window; the user may
move windows freely afterwards.

TO ARRANGE THE USER'S DESKTOPS ("organize my desktop/windows with deskmap"):
  1. Read the user's preferences first: LAYOUTS/README.md (if it exists).
     LAYOUTS = ~/Library/Application Support/Deskmap/layouts (layout files live there).
  2. Look at the current state:  deskmap status ; deskmap windows ; deskmap rules
  3. Write a layout file (YAML, format below), or edit an existing one in LAYOUTS.
     `deskmap dump --docked external/2 -o FILE` writes existing rules as a file.
  4. deskmap apply FILE --dry-run   shows rule changes and ⚠ warnings; show the
     user what will change before applying.
  5. deskmap apply FILE             edits the ACTIVE profile (other rules stay),
     reapplies and reports every window ✓/✗.  Undo: deskmap apply --undo
  6. deskmap check FILE             later: is everything still in place?
  Know:
  - Layout files are COPIES of rules; the user also edits rules in the app. If
    --dry-run shows a file would change rules the user did not ask about, the
    file is probably stale: ask before overwriting, refresh it with `dump`.
  - Editing means the ACTIVE profile. Only add `profile:`/`replace: true` when the
    user explicitly asks for another/new profile or a full replacement.
  - macOS cannot resize windows on a desktop that is not currently shown: those
    windows take their layout when the user next visits that desktop (✗ in the
    report until then). Do not switch desktops while the user is working.
  - A temporary pin (windows list: pin→) overrides rules; `deskmap unpin` it if
    the rule should win.
  - ⚠ "can be completely covered": with some stacking order a window would be
    fully hidden (less than 200x200 px of it is free of other windows).

LAYOUT FILE (YAML or JSON):
  profile: Name        # optional; default: active profile
  replace: false       # optional; true = the file is the profile's whole rule list
  desktops:            # optional desktop counts per mode and screen
    docked: {external: 4}
  windows:
    - app: Code                   # app name (or bundle: com.microsoft.VSCode)
      title: Orion-Makale     # optional title fragment(s), string or list
      docked: external/2 left-half            # "screen/desktop layout"
      # or an ordered list, one place per screen: the first connected one wins,
      # none connected → the first external monitor in role order
      #   docked: [external-2/1, external/2 left-half]
      undocked: {screen: builtin, desktop: 3, layout: {x: 0, y: 0, w: 0.7, h: 1}}
      place: builtin/1 full       # instead of docked+undocked: same for both
      launch: true                # open the app if no window is open (or a path/command)
  Layouts: a name (`deskmap layouts`) or x,y,w,h as fractions of the screen's
  usable area, top-left origin; `desktop-only` keeps the window's own frame. The most specific rule (most title fragments) wins.

COMMANDS:
  status | windows [--app A] | screens | rules | hooks      (--json for raw data)
  apply FILE [--dry-run] | apply FILE --remove | apply --undo | check FILE | dump
  layouts                          layout names
  screen-role DISPLAY ROLE | screen-role --forget   give a connected monitor (current role,
                                   UUID start or name) a role: external = 1, external-2 = 2 …;
                                   it keeps that role wherever it is placed (swaps if taken).
                                   A monitor Deskmap does not remember waits "on hold" (its
                                   layout is not applied) until it is given a role here
  screen-role DISPLAY --forget     forget one monitor: its role waits on hold again
  move W SCREEN [N] | pin W SCREEN [N] | unpin W            one window
  free W 15m|2h|lock|end           let a pinned window move freely for a while, until
                                   the screen locks, or end that early
  move W DESKTOP-NAME | pin W DESKTOP-NAME [--desktop-only] target by desktop name
                                   (--desktop-only: follow the desktop, keep position/size)
  desktops | name SCREEN N [NAME] [--mode M]  list desktop names | name a desktop (no NAME:
                                   remove). A name belongs to one desktop and follows it on any
                                   display; each setup has a plan (desktop order per display) that
                                   Deskmap applies on plug/unplug. Pins to a named desktop follow
                                   the name (`desktops` lists names, live places and plans).
  rule add --app A [--title T ...] --screen S [--desktop N] [--layout L|desktop-only]
           [--undocked-screen S --undocked-desktop N] | rule rm ID
  save-layout RULE [--window W]    use the window's current frame as the rule's layout
  pause | resume | toggle | reapply | reload | next-profile | profile NAME
  profile-rename OLD NEW | export FILE [--profile P]
  desktop-move SCREEN N M [--mode M]   reorder desktops (rules/pins/windows follow)
  backups [--json] | backup-now | backup-restore ID
                                   automatic backups of all profiles (hourly for 24 h,
                                   daily for 7 days, weekly forever); restore first backs
                                   up the current state and can be undone in the app
  W: window id or a unique app/title fragment. SCREEN: builtin, external,
  external-2… or part of the display name; each external monitor keeps the role
  it first got (or was given with `screen-role`), even if displays are rearranged.
  DESKTOP-NAME: a name given to a
  desktop (in the app: double-click "Desktop N" on the map, or `deskmap name`);
  exact or a unique part, case-insensitive. `pin` keeps the window there.
  `deskmap CMD --help` for options.

FILES: ~/Library/Application Support/Deskmap/: rules.json (rules, profiles),
status.json (live state), hooks.json (commands run when a window changes screen,
see docs/reference.md), apply-history/ (undo records), layouts/ (layout files),
Backups/ (automatic backups: hourly/, daily/, weekly/, pre-restore/).
"""
import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import urllib.parse
import uuid
from pathlib import Path

# DESKMAP_DATA_DIR: uygulamayla aynı veri klasörü (uçtan uca testler).
DIR = Path(os.environ.get("DESKMAP_DATA_DIR") or Path.home() / "Library/Application Support/Deskmap")
# DESKMAP_APP: URL'yi bu kopyaya gönder (birden çok Deskmap kopyası varken).
APP_PATH = os.environ.get("DESKMAP_APP")
STATUS = DIR / "status.json"
HOOKS = DIR / "hooks.json"
BACKUPS = DIR / "Backups"
BACKUP_TIERS = ("hourly", "daily", "weekly", "pre-restore")
TIMEOUT = 5.0


def die(message):
    print(f"deskmap: {message}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(1)


def running():
    return subprocess.run(["pgrep", "-x", "Deskmap"], capture_output=True).returncode == 0


def read_status():
    try:
        return json.loads(STATUS.read_text())
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return None
    except json.JSONDecodeError:
        time.sleep(0.1)  # yazılırken okunduysa bir kez daha
        return json.loads(STATUS.read_text())


def send(command, **query):
    """URL komutunu gönderir, işlenmesini bekler, güncel durumu döner."""
    if not running():
        die("Deskmap is not running")
    request = uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]
    query["req"] = request
    # quote (quote_plus değil): Foundation "+"yı boşluğa çevirmez.
    url = f"deskmap://{command}?{urllib.parse.urlencode(query, quote_via=urllib.parse.quote)}"
    subprocess.run(["open", "-g"] + (["-a", APP_PATH] if APP_PATH else []) + [url], check=True)
    deadline = time.time() + TIMEOUT
    while time.time() < deadline:
        status = read_status()
        if status and status.get("request") == request:
            if status.get("lastError"):
                die(status["lastError"])
            return status
        time.sleep(0.05)
    die(f"no answer from Deskmap within {TIMEOUT:.0f} s ({command})")


def fresh_status():
    if not running():
        die("Deskmap is not running")
    return send("status")


def resolve_screen(status, text):
    text_l = text.lower()
    screens = status["screens"]
    for s in screens:
        if s["id"] == text_l:
            return s["id"]
    hits = [s for s in screens if text_l in s["name"].lower()]
    if len(hits) == 1:
        return hits[0]["id"]
    if not hits:
        # Bağlı olmayan ekran da hedef olabilir (kural, ileride takılacak monitör).
        return text_l
    die(f"screen '{text}' is ambiguous: " + ", ".join(f"{s['id']} ({s['name']})" for s in hits))


def desktop_names(status):
    """[(ekran, masaüstü, ad)], ekran ve numara sırasıyla."""
    out = []
    for screen, names in (status.get("desktopNames") or {}).items():
        for n, name in names.items():
            out.append((screen, int(n), name))
    return sorted(out)


def find_desktop_name(status, text):
    """Ada göre (ekran, masaüstü); tam eşleşme önce, sonra tek parça eşleşmesi.
    Bulunamazsa None; birden çok parça eşleşmesi hata."""
    text_l = text.strip().lower()
    names = desktop_names(status)
    exact = [(sc, n) for sc, n, name in names if name.lower() == text_l]
    if len(exact) == 1:
        return exact[0]
    hits = exact or [(sc, n) for sc, n, name in names if text_l in name.lower()]
    if len(hits) == 1:
        return hits[0]
    if hits:
        die(f"desktop name '{text}' is ambiguous: " + ", ".join(
            f"{sc}/{n} ({name})" for sc, n, name in names if (sc, n) in hits))
    return None


def resolve_place(status, text, desktop):
    """SCREEN [N] ya da masaüstü adı → (ekran, masaüstü). Masaüstü numarası
    verilmediyse ve metin bir ekran kimliği değilse önce masaüstü adına bakılır."""
    ids = {s["id"] for s in status["screens"]}
    if desktop is None and text.lower() not in ids:
        named = find_desktop_name(status, text)
        if named:
            return named
        if not any(text.lower() in s["name"].lower() for s in status["screens"]):
            names = ", ".join(f"{name} ({sc}/{n})" for sc, n, name in desktop_names(status))
            die(f"no display or desktop named '{text}'"
                + (f"; desktop names: {names}" if names else ""))
    return resolve_screen(status, text), desktop or 1


def desktop_label(status, screen, desktop):
    name = ((status.get("desktopNames") or {}).get(screen) or {}).get(str(desktop))
    return f"{screen}/{desktop}" + (f" ({name})" if name else "")


def show_desktops(args):
    s = fresh_status()
    names = desktop_names(s)
    if args.json:
        print(json.dumps({"desktopNames": s.get("desktopNames") or {}, "names": s.get("names") or [],
                          "plans": s.get("plans") or {}}, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)); return
    ghosts = s.get("deletedDesktops") or []
    records = s.get("names")
    if not names and not ghosts and not records:
        print("(no desktop names; name one: deskmap name SCREEN N NAME)"); return
    if records is not None:
        # Şema 6: ad bir masaüstüne bağlı; yer canlı, plan kurulum başına.
        for r in sorted(records, key=lambda r: (r.get("screen") or "~", r.get("desktop") or 99, r["name"])):
            here = f"{r['screen']}/{r['desktop']}" if r.get("screen") else "(no desktop yet)"
            planned = ", ".join(f"{m}: {p}" for m, p in sorted((r.get("planned") or {}).items()))
            print(f"{here:<16} {r['name']}" + (f"   plan {planned}" if planned else ""))
        for mode, screens in sorted((s.get("plans") or {}).items()):
            ids = {r["id"]: r["name"] for r in records}
            for screen, entries in sorted(screens.items()):
                row = " | ".join(ids.get(e, "·") if e else "·" for e in entries)
                print(f"plan {mode}/{screen}: {row}")
    else:
        for sc, n, name in names:
            print(f"{sc + '/' + str(n):<14} {name}")
    for g in ghosts:
        apps = ", ".join(sorted({p["rule"]["appName"] for p in g.get("pins", [])}))
        print(f"{g['screen'] + ' deleted':<14} {g.get('name') or '(no name)'}"
              f"  — removed in Mission Control, {len(g.get('pins', []))} pin(s) kept: {apps or '-'}"
              "  (restore from the map)")


def name_desktop(args):
    s = fresh_status()
    screen = resolve_screen(s, args.screen)
    name = " ".join(args.name or [])
    query = {"name": name}
    if args.mode:
        query["mode"] = args.mode
    after = send(f"desktop-name/{screen}/{args.desktop}", **query)
    got = ((after.get("desktopNames") or {}).get(screen) or {}).get(str(args.desktop))
    if (not args.mode or args.mode == after.get("mode")) and (got or "") != name.strip():
        die("name was not saved")
    print(desktop_label(after, screen, args.desktop) if name.strip()
          else f"{screen}/{args.desktop}: name removed")


def resolve_window(status, text):
    windows = status["windows"]
    if text.isdigit():
        if any(w["id"] == int(text) for w in windows):
            return int(text)
        die(f"window {text} not found")
    text_l = text.lower()
    hits = [w for w in windows if text_l in w["app"].lower() or text_l in w["title"].lower()]
    if len(hits) == 1:
        return hits[0]["id"]
    if not hits:
        die(f"no window matches '{text}'")
    lines = "\n".join(f"  {w['id']}  {w['app']}: {w['title'][:60]}" for w in hits)
    die(f"'{text}' matches {len(hits)} windows, use an id:\n{lines}")


def where(w):
    if w["fullscreen"]:
        return f"{w['screen']} (fullscreen)"
    if w["minimized"]:
        return "minimized"
    if w.get("screen") is None:
        return "?"
    return f"{w['screen']}/{w['desktop']}"


def desktop_moves_text(state):
    """status.json `desktopMoves` → one line, or None when moves are on (or the
    app is older and does not report it)."""
    return {
        "held": "desktop moves OFF: not verified on this macOS (Try Anyway in the app turns them on)",
        "reduced": "desktop moves OFF: reduced mode, moves did not take effect (Try Again in the app)",
        "unavailable": "desktop moves OFF: not available on this macOS",
    }.get(state)


def show_status(args):
    s = fresh_status()
    if args.json:
        print(json.dumps(s, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)); return
    state = "routing" if s["enabled"] else "PAUSED"
    print(f"Deskmap pid {s['pid']}  {state}  mode {s['mode']}  profile {s.get('profile') or '-'}")
    moves = desktop_moves_text(s.get("desktopMoves"))
    if moves:
        print(f"  {moves}")
    for sc in s["screens"]:
        n = sum(1 for w in s["windows"] if w.get("screen") == sc["id"])
        print(f"  {sc['id']:<11} {sc['name']:<28} {n} window(s)")
    pins = sum(1 for w in s["windows"] if w.get("pinned"))
    print(f"  {len(s['windows'])} windows, {pins} pinned, {len(s['rules'])} rules")
    if s.get("perfFlags"):
        print(f"  perf flags on: {', '.join(s['perfFlags'])}")


def show_windows(args):
    s = fresh_status()
    windows = s["windows"]
    if args.app:
        windows = [w for w in windows if args.app.lower() in w["app"].lower()]
    if args.json:
        print(json.dumps(windows, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)); return
    for w in windows:
        pin = f"  pin→{w['pinned']['screen']}/{w['pinned']['desktop']}" if w.get("pinned") else ""
        place = where(w)
        if w.get("desktop") and w.get("screen") and not w["fullscreen"] and not w["minimized"]:
            place = desktop_label(s, w["screen"], w["desktop"])
        key = f"  key={w['key']}" if w.get("key") else "  key=-"
        # Pinin kullanılan yeri: sıradaki yer (1, 2 …), fallback ya da untouched.
        used = f"  place={w['place']}" if w.get("place") else ""
        print(f"{w['id']:>7}  {w['app'][:18]:<18} {place[:28]:<28} {w['title'][:50]}{pin}{key}{used}")


def show_screens(args):
    s = fresh_status()
    if args.json:
        print(json.dumps(s["screens"], indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)); return
    remembered = (s.get("displayRoles") or {}).get("remembered") or {}
    held = set(s.get("heldRoles") or [])
    for sc in s["screens"]:
        x, y, w, h = sc["frame"]
        uuid = sc.get("uuid", "")
        kept = "" if sc["builtin"] else (
            f"  role on hold: layout not applied (confirm: deskmap screen-role {uuid[:8]} {sc['id']})"
            if sc["id"] in held else
            "  role kept" if uuid in remembered.get(sc["id"], []) else "  role by position")
        print(f"{sc['id']:<11} {sc['name']:<28} {int(w)}x{int(h)} at {int(x)},{int(y)}"
              f"  {uuid[:8]}{kept}")
        for n, name in sorted(((int(k), v) for k, v in
                               ((s.get("desktopNames") or {}).get(sc["id"]) or {}).items())):
            print(f"    desktop {n}: {name}")


def dest_text(d):
    if not d:
        return "-"
    lay = d.get("layout") or {}
    full = all(lay.get(k) == v for k, v in (("x", 0), ("y", 0), ("w", 1), ("h", 1)))
    return f"{d['screen']}/{d['desktop']}" + ("" if full else
        f" [{lay.get('x', 0):g},{lay.get('y', 0):g},{lay.get('w', 1):g},{lay.get('h', 1):g}]")


def docked_places(r):
    """Monitörlü sıralı yerler: `docked` ilk, `dockedNext` sonrakiler."""
    return ([r["docked"]] if r.get("docked") else []) + list(r.get("dockedNext") or [])


def external_index(role):
    if role == "external":
        return 1
    head, _, n = role.partition("external-")
    return int(n) if not head and n.isdigit() and int(n) >= 2 else None


def effective_place(status, r):
    """Pencerenin bu durumda gideceği yer (Deskmap'in `Routing.resolvePlace`'i
    gibi): bağlı ve onay beklemeyen ekrandaki ilk yer; yoksa rol sırasında
    bağlı ilk harici ekran, ilk yerin masaüstü numarasıyla. Adlı masaüstü
    önbellekteki ekranına göre sayılır. Yer yoksa None."""
    mode = status.get("mode", "docked")
    places = docked_places(r) if mode == "docked" else ([r[mode]] if r.get(mode) else [])
    usable = {sc["id"] for sc in status.get("screens", [])} - set(status.get("heldRoles") or [])
    counts = {sc["id"]: sc.get("desktops") for sc in status.get("screens", [])}

    def clamped(d):
        # Ekranda o kadar masaüstü yoksa Deskmap son masaüstüne koyar.
        count = counts.get(d["screen"])
        return {**d, "desktop": min(d["desktop"], count)} if count else d
    for d in places:
        if d["screen"] in usable:
            return clamped(d)
    externals = sorted((external_index(x), x) for x in usable if external_index(x))
    if not places or not externals:
        return None
    return clamped({**places[0], "screen": externals[0][1]})


def docked_text(r):
    places = docked_places(r)
    return " → ".join(dest_text(d) for d in places) if places else "-"


def place_item(d):
    """Düzen dosyasındaki yazımı: 'ekran/N düzen' ya da sözlük."""
    lay = layout_name(d.get("layout") or {})
    return (f"{d['screen']}/{d['desktop']} {lay}" if isinstance(lay, str)
            else {"screen": d["screen"], "desktop": d["desktop"], "layout": lay})


def docked_item(r):
    """Düzen dosyasına `docked`: tek yer ya da sıralı liste."""
    places = [place_item(d) for d in docked_places(r)]
    return places[0] if len(places) == 1 else places


def show_rules(args):
    s = fresh_status()
    if args.json:
        print(json.dumps(s["rules"], indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)); return
    for r in s["rules"]:
        title = f" title~{' '.join(r['tokens'])}" if r.get("tokens") else ""
        if r.get("path"):
            title += f" file={r['path']}"
        print(f"{r['id']}  {r['appName']}{title}\n    docked {docked_text(r)}"
              f"  undocked {dest_text(r.get('undocked'))}")


def show_hooks(args):
    if not HOOKS.exists():
        print("(no hooks.json)"); return
    print(HOOKS.read_text().rstrip())


def backup_entries():
    """Uygulamanın yazdığı yedekler (en yeni önce); okunamayanlar atlanır."""
    entries = []
    for tier in BACKUP_TIERS:
        folder = BACKUPS / tier
        if not folder.is_dir():
            continue
        for path in folder.glob(f"{tier}-*.json"):
            try:
                bundle = json.loads(path.read_text())
                doc = json.loads(bundle["files"]["rules.json"])
            except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
                continue
            if bundle.get("kind") != "deskmap-backup":
                continue
            active = doc.get("activeProfileID")
            profiles = [{"name": pr.get("name", ""), "rules": len(pr.get("rules", [])),
                         "active": pr.get("id") == active} for pr in doc.get("profiles", [])]
            entries.append({"id": path.stem, "tier": tier, "created": bundle.get("created", ""),
                            "profiles": profiles})
    entries.sort(key=lambda e: (e["created"], e["id"]), reverse=True)
    return entries


def show_backups(args):
    entries = backup_entries()
    if args.json:
        print(json.dumps(entries, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)); return
    if not entries:
        print("(no backups yet)"); return
    for tier in BACKUP_TIERS:
        rows = [e for e in entries if e["tier"] == tier]
        if not rows:
            continue
        print(f"{tier}:")
        for e in rows:
            profiles = ", ".join(f"{'*' if p['active'] else ''}{p['name']} ({p['rules']})"
                                 for p in e["profiles"])
            print(f"  {e['id']:<34} {e['created']:<21} {profiles}")


def backup_restore(args):
    if args.id not in {e["id"] for e in backup_entries()}:
        die(f"backup not found: {args.id} (see `deskmap backups`)")
    send(f"backup-restore/{urllib.parse.quote(args.id, safe='')}")
    print(f"restored {args.id} (the previous state is in pre-restore/; Undo in the app)")


def layout(text):
    try:
        return parse_layout(text)
    except ValueError as error:
        die(str(error))


_BUNDLES = {}


def bundle_id(app):
    """Bundle id of an installed app by name; '' if not found.

    Rules without one match by name only, Safari reopen skips its own path and
    the map puts them in a separate app group."""
    if app not in _BUNDLES:
        import plistlib
        found = ""
        try:  # running apps first: process names differ from .app names (Code)
            with open(STATUS) as f:
                for w in json.load(f).get("windows", []):
                    if w.get("app") == app and w.get("bundleID"):
                        found = w["bundleID"]
                        break
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            pass
        for root in () if found else ("/Applications", "/System/Applications",
                     "/System/Applications/Utilities", "/System/Volumes/Preboot/Cryptexes/App/System/Applications",
                     str(Path.home() / "Applications")):
            plist = Path(root) / f"{app}.app" / "Contents" / "Info.plist"
            try:
                with open(plist, "rb") as f:
                    found = plistlib.load(f).get("CFBundleIdentifier", "")
            except (OSError, plistlib.InvalidFileException):
                continue
            if found:
                break
        _BUNDLES[app] = found
    return _BUNDLES[app]


def rule_add(args):
    s = fresh_status()
    if not args.screen and not args.undocked_screen:
        die("give --screen and/or --undocked-screen")
    lay = layout(args.layout) if args.layout else {"x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 1, "h": 1}
    rule = {"id": str(uuid.uuid4()).upper(), "appName": args.app,
            "bundleID": args.bundle or bundle_id(args.app), "tokens": args.title or []}
    if args.screen:
        screen, desktop = resolve_place(s, args.screen, args.desktop)
        rule["docked"] = {"screen": screen, "desktop": desktop, "layout": lay}
    if args.undocked_screen:
        screen, desktop = resolve_place(s, args.undocked_screen, args.undocked_desktop)
        rule["undocked"] = {"screen": screen, "desktop": desktop, "layout": lay}
    after = send("rule-add", json=json.dumps(rule, separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False))
    if not any(r["id"] == rule["id"] for r in after["rules"]):
        die("rule was not added")
    print(rule["id"])


def rule_rm(args):
    after = send(f"rule-remove/{args.id}")
    if any(r["id"] == args.id for r in after["rules"]):
        die("rule is still there")


def free_duration(text):
    """'15m', '2h', '30' (minutes), 'lock' or 'end' → minutes, "lock" or "end"."""
    d = text.strip().lower()
    if d in ("end", "lock"):
        return d
    m = re.fullmatch(r"(\d+)\s*(m|min|h)?", d)
    if not m or int(m.group(1)) <= 0:
        raise ValueError("duration: e.g. 15m, 2h, lock or end")
    return int(m.group(1)) * (60 if m.group(2) == "h" else 1)


def free_move(args):
    s = fresh_status()
    window = resolve_window(s, args.window)
    try:
        d = free_duration(args.duration)
    except ValueError as error:
        die(str(error))
    if d == "end":
        send(f"free-end/{window}")
    else:
        send(f"free/{window}/{d}")
    w = next((w for w in fresh_status()["windows"] if w["id"] == window), None)
    free = w and w.get("free")
    if d == "end":
        print(f"{window}: free move ended" if not free else die("free move is still active"))
    elif not free:
        die(f"{window}: no free move (is the window pinned?)")
    else:
        if free == "lock":
            print(f"{window}: free until the screen locks")
        else:
            from datetime import datetime
            local = datetime.fromisoformat(free.replace("Z", "+00:00")).astimezone()
            print(f"{window}: free until {local:%H:%M:%S}")


def window_command(name):
    def run(args):
        s = fresh_status()
        window = resolve_window(s, args.window)
        if name == "unpin":
            send(f"unpin/{window}")
        else:
            screen, desktop = resolve_place(s, args.screen, args.desktop)
            extra = {"layout": "desktop-only"} if getattr(args, "desktop_only", False) else {}
            send(f"{name}/{window}/{screen}/{desktop}", **extra)
            print(f"{window} → {desktop_label(s, screen, desktop)}"
                  + (" (pinned until the window closes)" if name == "pin" else ""))
        if name == "move":
            # Taşıma arka planda; sonucu bir sonraki taramada görünür.
            time.sleep(1.0)
            w = next((w for w in fresh_status()["windows"] if w["id"] == window), None)
            print(f"{window}: {where(w) if w else 'gone'}")
    return run


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- düzen dosyası

NAMED_LAYOUTS = {
    "full": (0, 0, 1, 1), "center": (0.1, 0.1, 0.8, 0.8),
    "left-half": (0, 0, 0.5, 1), "right-half": (0.5, 0, 0.5, 1),
    "top-half": (0, 0, 1, 0.5), "bottom-half": (0, 0.5, 1, 0.5),
    "left-third": (0, 0, 1 / 3, 1), "center-third": (1 / 3, 0, 1 / 3, 1),
    "right-third": (2 / 3, 0, 1 / 3, 1),
    "left-two-thirds": (0, 0, 2 / 3, 1), "right-two-thirds": (1 / 3, 0, 2 / 3, 1),
    "center-two-thirds": (1 / 6, 0, 2 / 3, 1),
    "top-left": (0, 0, 0.5, 0.5), "top-right": (0.5, 0, 0.5, 0.5),
    "bottom-left": (0, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5), "bottom-right": (0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5),
    "left-quarter": (0, 0, 0.25, 1), "right-quarter": (0.75, 0, 0.25, 1),
}
# Yalnız masaüstü: pencere masaüstünü izler, konum/boyut serbest.
DESKTOP_ONLY = {"x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 1, "h": 1, "desktopOnly": True}
HISTORY = DIR / "apply-history"
MODES = ("docked", "undocked")


def parse_layout(value):
    """Ad (left-half…), "x,y,w,h" metni ya da {x,y,w,h} → {x,y,w,h}."""
    if value is None:
        value = "full"
    if isinstance(value, dict) and value.get("desktopOnly"):
        return dict(DESKTOP_ONLY)
    if isinstance(value, dict):
        # Sabit boyutlu yerleşim (Deskmap'in "fixed" alanı) olduğu gibi korunur.
        try:
            out = {k: float(value[k]) for k in ("x", "y", "w", "h")}
        except (KeyError, ValueError):
            raise ValueError(f"layout needs x, y, w, h: {value}")
        if value.get("fixed"):
            f = value["fixed"]
            if not {"anchor", "width", "height"} <= set(f):
                raise ValueError(f"fixed needs anchor, width, height: {f}")
            out["fixed"] = {"anchor": str(f["anchor"]), "width": float(f["width"]),
                            "height": float(f["height"])}
        return out
    text = str(value).strip().lower()
    if text == "desktop-only":
        return dict(DESKTOP_ONLY)
    if text in NAMED_LAYOUTS:
        x, y, w, h = NAMED_LAYOUTS[text]
    else:
        try:
            x, y, w, h = (float(v) for v in text.split(","))
        except ValueError:
            raise ValueError(f"unknown layout '{value}' (names: {', '.join(NAMED_LAYOUTS)})")
    if not (0 <= x < 1 and 0 <= y < 1 and 0 < w <= 1 and 0 < h <= 1 and x + w <= 1.001 and y + h <= 1.001):
        raise ValueError(f"layout out of range: {value}")
    return {"x": x, "y": y, "w": w, "h": h}


def parse_place(value):
    """'external/2 left-half' ya da {screen, desktop, layout} → hedef."""
    if value is None:
        return None
    if isinstance(value, str):
        parts = value.split()
        if not parts:
            raise ValueError("empty placement")
        screen, _, desktop = parts[0].partition("/")
        value = {"screen": screen, "desktop": int(desktop or 1),
                 "layout": parts[1] if len(parts) > 1 else "full"}
    if "screen" not in value:
        raise ValueError(f"placement needs a screen: {value}")
    desktop = int(value.get("desktop", 1))
    if desktop < 1:
        raise ValueError(f"desktop must be ≥ 1: {value}")
    return {"screen": str(value["screen"]).lower(), "desktop": desktop,
            "layout": parse_layout(value.get("layout"))}


def load_spec(path):
    text = Path(path).read_text()
    if path.endswith((".yaml", ".yml")):
        try:
            import yaml
        except ImportError:
            die("YAML needs PyYAML (pip install pyyaml) or use a .json file")
        spec = yaml.safe_load(text)
    else:
        spec = json.loads(text)
    if not isinstance(spec, dict):
        die("layout file must be a mapping (profile/desktops/windows)")
    return spec


def build_plan(spec):
    """Düzen dosyası → profil kuralları, masaüstü sayıları, açılacak uygulamalar."""
    rules, launches, errors = [], [], []
    for i, item in enumerate(spec.get("windows") or [], 1):
        try:
            if not item.get("app"):
                raise ValueError("needs 'app'")
            title = item.get("title") or []
            tokens = [title] if isinstance(title, str) else [str(t) for t in title]
            rule = {"id": str(uuid.uuid4()).upper(), "appName": item["app"],
                    "bundleID": item.get("bundle") or bundle_id(item["app"]), "tokens": tokens}
            both = item.get("place")
            for mode in MODES:
                value = item.get(mode, both)
                if isinstance(value, list):
                    # Monitörlü sıralı yerler (bağlı ilk yer kazanır); laptop tek yer.
                    if mode != "docked" or item.get(mode) is None:
                        raise ValueError("only 'docked' takes a list of places")
                    places = [parse_place(v) for v in value]
                    if len({d["screen"] for d in places}) != len(places):
                        raise ValueError("docked: one place per screen")
                    if places:
                        rule["docked"] = places[0]
                    if len(places) > 1:
                        rule["dockedNext"] = places[1:]
                    continue
                place = parse_place(value)
                if place:
                    rule[mode] = place
            if not any(m in rule for m in MODES):
                raise ValueError("needs 'docked', 'undocked' or 'place'")
            rules.append(rule)
            if item.get("launch"):
                launches.append({"app": item["app"], "bundle": item.get("bundle"),
                                 "launch": item["launch"], "tokens": tokens})
        except (ValueError, TypeError) as error:
            errors.append(f"windows[{i}] ({item.get('app', '?') if isinstance(item, dict) else item}): {error}")
    desktops = []
    for mode, screens in (spec.get("desktops") or {}).items():
        if mode not in MODES:
            errors.append(f"desktops: unknown mode '{mode}' (docked/undocked)")
            continue
        for screen, count in (screens or {}).items():
            if not isinstance(count, int) or not 1 <= count <= 16:
                errors.append(f"desktops.{mode}.{screen}: count must be 1…16")
            else:
                desktops.append((mode, str(screen).lower(), count))
    if errors:
        die("layout file errors:\n  " + "\n  ".join(errors))
    return {"profile": str(spec["profile"]) if spec.get("profile") else None,
            "replace": bool(spec.get("replace")), "rules": rules,
            "desktops": desktops, "launches": launches}


def merge_rules(old, new, replace):
    """Varsayılan: profilin öteki kuralları kalır; dosyadaki pencerenin kuralı
    (aynı uygulama + başlık parçaları) güncellenir, yoksa eklenir. Güncellenen
    kural kimliğini korur. `replace` ise liste dosyadakiyle değişir."""
    if replace or not old:
        return [dict(r) for r in new], [r["id"] for r in new]
    merged = [dict(r) for r in old]
    index = {rule_key(r): i for i, r in enumerate(merged)}
    ids = []
    for r in new:
        i = index.get(rule_key(r))
        if i is None:
            merged.append(dict(r))
            ids.append(r["id"])
        else:
            # Dosyada yazmayan modun hedefi korunur (ör. yalnız docked verilmişse
            # undocked kalır); kimlik de korunur.
            old_rule = merged[i]
            if "docked" in r:
                # Monitörlü liste bütün olarak dosyadakiyle değişir.
                old_rule = {k: v for k, v in old_rule.items() if k != "dockedNext"}
            merged[i] = {**old_rule,
                         **{k: v for k, v in r.items() if k not in MODES and k not in ("id", "dockedNext")},
                         **{m: r[m] for m in MODES if m in r},
                         **({"dockedNext": r["dockedNext"]} if r.get("dockedNext") else {})}
            ids.append(old_rule["id"])
    return merged, ids


def rule_key(r):
    return (r["appName"].lower(), r.get("bundleID", ""), tuple(t.lower() for t in r.get("tokens", [])),
            r.get("path"))


def profile_rules(name):
    """Profilin diskteki kuralları (yoksa None). Etkin profilin canlı hâli status'ta."""
    try:
        doc = json.loads((DIR / "rules.json").read_text())
    except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError):
        return None
    for p in doc.get("profiles", []):
        if p.get("name") == name:
            if p.get("id") == doc.get("activeProfileID"):
                return doc.get("rules", p.get("rules", []))
            return p.get("rules", [])
    return None


def place_text(d):
    return dest_text(d) if d else "-"


def diff_rules(old, new):
    old_by, new_by = {rule_key(r): r for r in old or []}, {rule_key(r): r for r in new}
    lines = []
    for k, r in new_by.items():
        label = r["appName"] + (f" ~{' '.join(r['tokens'])}" if r["tokens"] else "")
        before = old_by.get(k)
        now = f"docked {docked_text(r)}, undocked {place_text(r.get('undocked'))}"
        if not before:
            lines.append(f"  + {label}: {now}")
        elif (docked_places(before) != docked_places(r)
              or before.get("undocked") != r.get("undocked")):
            was = f"docked {docked_text(before)}, undocked {place_text(before.get('undocked'))}"
            lines.append(f"  ~ {label}: {was}  →  {now}")
    for k, r in old_by.items():
        if k not in new_by:
            lines.append(f"  - {r['appName']}" + (f" ~{' '.join(r['tokens'])}" if r.get("tokens") else ""))
    return lines


def app_running(entry, status):
    name, tokens = entry["app"].lower(), [t.lower() for t in entry["tokens"]]
    return any(w["app"].lower() == name and all(t in w["title"].lower() for t in tokens)
               for w in status["windows"])


def launch(entry):
    how = entry["launch"]
    if how is True:
        cmd = ["open", "-g", "-b", entry["bundle"]] if entry.get("bundle") else ["open", "-g", "-a", entry["app"]]
    elif isinstance(how, str) and how.startswith(("/", "~")):
        cmd = ["open", "-g", "-a", entry["app"], str(Path(how).expanduser())]
    else:
        cmd = ["/bin/sh", "-c", str(how)]
    result = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)
    return result.returncode == 0, (result.stderr or "").strip()


def target_rect(status, screen_id, layout):
    if layout.get("desktopOnly"):
        return None
    sc = next((s for s in status["screens"] if s["id"] == screen_id), None)
    if not sc or "visible" not in sc:
        return None
    x, y, w, h = sc["visible"]
    primary = status.get("primaryHeight") or next(
        (s["frame"][3] for s in status["screens"] if s["frame"][:2] == [0, 0]), 0)
    top = primary - (y + h)
    return [x + layout["x"] * w, top + layout["y"] * h, layout["w"] * w, layout["h"] * h]


def specificity(r):
    """Deskmap'in sırası: belge yollu kural önce, sonra çok parçalı."""
    return -(len(r.get("tokens", [])) + (1000 if r.get("path") else 0))


def rule_label(r):
    text = r["appName"] + (f" ~{' '.join(r['tokens'])}" if r.get("tokens") else "")
    return text + (f" file={os.path.basename(r['path'])}" if r.get("path") else "")


def rule_matches(r, w):
    if r.get("bundleID"):
        if w["bundleID"] != r["bundleID"]:
            return False
    elif w["app"].lower() != r["appName"].lower():
        return False
    if r.get("path") and w.get("document") != r["path"]:
        return False
    return all(t.lower() in w["title"].lower() for t in r.get("tokens", []))


def report(status, rules, only=None):
    """Etkin moddaki pencereler kurallarının hedefinde mi. Seçim Deskmap'inki
    gibi: oturum pini önce, sonra en çok başlık parçalı uyan kural."""
    mode = status["mode"]
    ordered = sorted((r for r in rules if r.get(mode)), key=specificity)
    label = rule_label
    rows, ok_count, total, used = [], 0, 0, set()
    for w in status["windows"]:
        if w["minimized"]:
            continue
        r = next((r for r in ordered if rule_matches(r, w)), None)
        if not r or (only is not None and r["id"] not in only):
            continue
        used.add(r["id"])
        total += 1
        if w.get("pinned"):
            rows.append(f"  ·  {label(r)} [{w['id']}]: temporary pin wins ({w['pinned']['screen']}/{w['pinned']['desktop']})")
            total -= 1
            continue
        dest = effective_place(status, r)
        if dest is None:
            # Sıralı yerlerin hiçbiri bağlı değil ve yedek de yok: dokunulmaz.
            rows.append(f"  ·  {label(r)} [{w['id']}]: no connected place (left alone)")
            total -= 1
            continue
        problems = []
        if w.get("fullscreen"):
            problems.append("fullscreen (Deskmap leaves it alone)")
        elif w.get("screen") != dest["screen"] or w.get("desktop") != dest["desktop"]:
            problems.append(f"at {where(w)}, want {dest['screen']}/{dest['desktop']}")
        want = target_rect(status, dest["screen"], dest["layout"])
        if want and w.get("frame") and not problems:
            off = max(abs(a - b) for a, b in zip(w["frame"], want))
            if off > 40:
                problems.append("size/position off by %dpx (want %dx%d at %d,%d, is %dx%d at %d,%d)"
                                % (off, want[2], want[3], want[0], want[1],
                                   w["frame"][2], w["frame"][3], w["frame"][0], w["frame"][1]))
        title = f" \"{w['title'][:40]}\"" if not r.get("tokens") else ""
        if problems:
            rows.append(f"  ✗  {label(r)} [{w['id']}]{title}: " + "; ".join(problems))
        else:
            ok_count += 1
            rows.append(f"  ✓  {label(r)} [{w['id']}]{title}: {dest['screen']}/{dest['desktop']}")
    for r in ordered:
        if r["id"] not in used and (only is None or r["id"] in only):
            rows.append(f"  ·  {label(r)}: no open window")
    return ok_count, total, rows


EXPOSED_MIN = 200   # px: her pencerenin hiçbir şeyin altında kalmayan en az bu kadar karesi
GRID = 20


def exposure_issues(status, rules, desks=None):
    """Etkin modda açık pencerelerin hedef dikdörtgenleri: hangi pencere,
    ön/arka sırasından bağımsız olarak tamamen örtülebilir (EXPOSED_MIN
    karelik açık alanı yok). Ekran ve masaüstü başına bakılır."""
    mode = status["mode"]
    ordered = sorted((r for r in rules if r.get(mode)), key=specificity)
    groups = {}
    for w in status["windows"]:
        if w["minimized"] or w.get("fullscreen"):
            continue
        r = next((r for r in ordered if rule_matches(r, w)), None)
        if w.get("pinned"):
            dest = {"screen": w["pinned"]["screen"], "desktop": w["pinned"]["desktop"], "layout": None}
            label = f"{w['app']} [{w['id']}] (temporary pin)"
        elif r:
            dest = effective_place(status, r)
            if dest is None:
                continue
            label = r["appName"] + (f" ~{' '.join(r['tokens'])}" if r.get("tokens") else "")
        else:
            continue
        rect = target_rect(status, dest["screen"], dest["layout"]) if dest.get("layout") else w.get("frame")
        if rect:
            groups.setdefault((dest["screen"], dest["desktop"]), {})[label] = rect
    issues = []
    block = EXPOSED_MIN // GRID
    for (screen, desktop), rects in sorted(groups.items()):
        if desks is not None and (screen, desktop) not in desks:
            continue
        cells = {}
        for label, (x, y, w, h) in rects.items():
            for cx in range(int(x // GRID), int((x + w) // GRID)):
                for cy in range(int(y // GRID), int((y + h) // GRID)):
                    cells.setdefault((cx, cy), set()).add(label)
        for label, (x, y, w, h) in rects.items():
            own = {c for c, owners in cells.items() if owners == {label}}
            ok = any(all((cx + i, cy + j) in own for i in range(block) for j in range(block))
                     for cx, cy in own)
            if not ok:
                issues.append(f"{screen}/{desktop}: {label} can be completely covered")
    return issues


def apply_layout(args):
    if args.undo:
        return apply_undo()
    spec = load_spec(args.file)
    plan = build_plan(spec)
    status = fresh_status()
    # Profil yazılmadıysa etkin profil değişir.
    name = plan["profile"] or status.get("profile")
    if not name:
        die("no active profile; name one with 'profile:'")
    old = profile_rules(name)
    if args.remove:
        if old is None:
            die(f"profile '{name}' does not exist")
        gone = {rule_key(r) for r in plan["rules"]}
        rules, file_ids = [r for r in old if rule_key(r) not in gone], []
        plan["desktops"], plan["launches"] = [], []
        missing = len(gone) - (len(old) - len(rules))
        if missing:
            print(f"  note: {missing} rule(s) from the file are not in the profile")
    else:
        rules, file_ids = merge_rules(old, plan["rules"], plan["replace"])
    kind = "new" if old is None else ("remove" if args.remove else "replace" if plan["replace"] else "edit")
    active = " (active)" if name == status.get("profile") else ""
    print(f"Profile '{name}'{active}: {kind}, {len(plan['rules'])} rule(s) from file, "
          f"{len(rules)} in profile; mode {status['mode']}")
    changes = diff_rules(old, rules)
    print("\n".join(changes) if changes else "  (rules unchanged)")
    for mode, screen, count in plan["desktops"]:
        print(f"  desktops {mode} {screen}: {count}")
    pending = [e for e in plan["launches"] if not app_running(e, status)]
    for e in pending:
        print(f"  launch {e['app']}" + (f" ({e['launch']})" if e["launch"] is not True else ""))
    # Gerçek hedefe göre (exposure_issues ile aynı yer kavramı)
    desks = {(d["screen"], d["desktop"]) for d in
             (effective_place(status, r) for r in plan["rules"] if r.get(status["mode"])) if d}
    for issue in exposure_issues(status, rules, desks):
        print(f"  ⚠ {issue}")
    if args.dry_run:
        print("(dry run, nothing changed)")
        return
    HISTORY.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    record = {"time": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S"), "file": str(Path(args.file).resolve()),
              "previousProfile": status.get("profile"), "profile": name, "previousRules": old}
    stamp = time.strftime("%Y%m%d-%H%M%S")
    (HISTORY / f"{stamp}.json").write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False))
    for e in pending:
        ok, err = launch(e)
        print(f"  launched {e['app']}" if ok else f"  could not launch {e['app']}: {err}")
    for mode, screen, count in plan["desktops"]:
        send(f"plan-desktops/{screen}/{count}", mode=mode)
    profile = {"name": name, "rules": rules}
    send("profile-set", json=json.dumps(profile, separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False), activate="1")
    send("reapply")
    wait = args.wait if pending else min(args.wait, 4.0)
    time.sleep(wait)
    after = fresh_status()
    ok_count, total, rows = report(after, rules, only=set(file_ids))
    print(f"Result ({after['mode']}): {ok_count}/{total} window(s) in place")
    print("\n".join(rows))
    print(f"undo: deskmap apply --undo   (record {HISTORY / (stamp + '.json')})")
    if ok_count < total:
        sys.exit(2)


def apply_undo():
    records = sorted(HISTORY.glob("*.json")) if HISTORY.exists() else []
    if not records:
        die("nothing to undo")
    last = records[-1]
    rec = json.loads(last.read_text())
    if rec.get("previousRules") is not None:
        send("profile-set", json=json.dumps({"name": rec["profile"], "rules": rec["previousRules"]},
                                            separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False))
    if rec.get("previousProfile"):
        send("profile", name=rec["previousProfile"])
    send("reapply")
    last.rename(last.with_suffix(".undone"))
    print(f"restored profile '{rec.get('previousProfile')}'"
          + ("" if rec.get("previousRules") is None else f", '{rec['profile']}' rules reverted"))


def layout_name(lay):
    """Hazır ada denk düşen yerleşimin adı, yoksa sözlüğün kendisi."""
    if lay.get("desktopOnly"):
        return "desktop-only"
    if not lay.get("fixed"):
        for name, xywh in NAMED_LAYOUTS.items():
            if all(abs(lay.get(k, 0) - v) < 1e-4 for k, v in zip("xywh", xywh)):
                return name
    out = {k: lay.get(k, 0) for k in "xywh"}
    if lay.get("fixed"):
        f = lay["fixed"]
        out["fixed"] = {"anchor": f["anchor"], "width": f["width"], "height": f["height"]}
    return out


def dump_layout(args):
    """Etkin profilin seçilen kurallarını düzen dosyası olarak yazar."""
    s = fresh_status()
    picked = []
    for r in s["rules"]:
        hit = False
        for spec, mode in ((args.docked, "docked"), (args.undocked, "undocked")):
            for target in spec or []:
                scr, _, desk = target.partition("/")
                places = docked_places(r) if mode == "docked" else [r[mode]] if r.get(mode) else []
                if any(d["screen"] == scr.lower() and (not desk or d["desktop"] == int(desk))
                       for d in places):
                    hit = True
        if args.title and any(t.lower() in " ".join(r.get("tokens", [])).lower() for t in args.title):
            hit = True
        if hit:
            picked.append(r)
    windows = []
    for r in picked:
        item = {"app": r["appName"]}
        if r.get("bundleID"):
            item["bundle"] = r["bundleID"]
        if r.get("tokens"):
            item["title"] = r["tokens"][0] if len(r["tokens"]) == 1 else r["tokens"]
        if docked_places(r):
            item["docked"] = docked_item(r)
        if r.get("undocked"):
            item["undocked"] = place_item(r["undocked"])
        windows.append(item)
    if not windows:
        die("no rule matches")
    try:
        import yaml

        class Dumper(yaml.SafeDumper):
            pass
        # Yerleşim sözlükleri tek satırda: {x: 0, y: 0, w: 0.5, h: 1}
        Dumper.add_representer(dict, lambda d, data: d.represent_mapping(
            "tag:yaml.org,2002:map", data.items(),
            flow_style=set(data) <= {"x", "y", "w", "h", "fixed", "anchor", "width", "height"}))
        text = yaml.dump({"windows": windows}, Dumper=Dumper, allow_unicode=True,
                         sort_keys=False, width=120)
    except ImportError:
        text = json.dumps({"windows": windows}, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n"
    header = f"# {s.get('profile')} profilinden, {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}\n"
    if args.output:
        Path(args.output).expanduser().write_text(header + text)
        print(f"{len(windows)} rule(s) → {args.output}")
    else:
        print(header + text, end="")


def check_layout(args):
    """Düzen dosyasını uygulamadan, şu anki pencerelere göre raporla."""
    plan = build_plan(load_spec(args.file))
    status = fresh_status()
    name = plan["profile"] or status.get("profile")
    rules, ids = merge_rules(profile_rules(name), plan["rules"], plan["replace"])
    if name != status.get("profile"):
        print(f"(profile '{name}' is not active; showing where its rules would apply)")
    ok_count, total, rows = report(status, rules, only=set(ids))
    print(f"{ok_count}/{total} window(s) in place ({status['mode']})")
    print("\n".join(rows))
    # Gerçek hedefe göre (exposure_issues ile aynı yer kavramı)
    desks = {(d["screen"], d["desktop"]) for d in
             (effective_place(status, r) for r in plan["rules"] if r.get(status["mode"])) if d}
    issues = exposure_issues(status, rules, desks)
    for issue in issues:
        print(f"  ⚠ {issue}")
    if issues:
        sys.exit(2)
    sys.exit(0 if ok_count == total else 2)


def resolve_rule(status, text):
    rules = status["rules"]
    if any(r["id"] == text for r in rules):
        return text
    t = text.lower()
    hits = [r for r in rules if t == r["appName"].lower()
            or t in (r["appName"] + " " + " ".join(r.get("tokens", []))).lower()]
    if len(hits) == 1:
        return hits[0]["id"]
    if not hits:
        die(f"no rule matches '{text}'")
    lines = "\n".join(f"  {r['id']}  {r['appName']} {' '.join(r.get('tokens', []))}" for r in hits)
    die(f"'{text}' matches {len(hits)} rules, use an id:\n{lines}")


def export_profile(args):
    path = str(Path(args.file).expanduser().resolve())
    query = {"path": path}
    if args.profile:
        query["name"] = args.profile
    send("profile-export", **query)
    print(path)


def desktop_move(args):
    s = fresh_status()
    query = {"mode": args.mode} if args.mode else {}
    send(f"desktop-move/{resolve_screen(s, args.screen)}/{args.src}/{args.dst}", **query)


def save_layout(args):
    s = fresh_status()
    rule = resolve_rule(s, args.rule)
    before = next(r for r in s["rules"] if r["id"] == rule).get(s["mode"])
    query = {"window": str(resolve_window(s, args.window))} if args.window else {}
    after = send(f"rule-save-layout/{rule}", **query)
    now = next(r for r in after["rules"] if r["id"] == rule).get(after["mode"])
    print(f"{place_text(before)}  →  {place_text(now)}")


def role_name(text):
    """'2' / 'monitor-2' / 'external-2' → 'external-2'; '1' → 'external'."""
    t = text.strip().lower().removeprefix("monitor").strip(" -")
    if t.isdigit():
        return "external" if int(t) <= 1 else f"external-{int(t)}"
    if t == "external" or (t.startswith("external-") and t[9:].isdigit() and int(t[9:]) >= 2):
        return t
    die(f"'{text}' is not an external role (external, external-2, … or 1, 2, …)")


def screen_role(args):
    if args.forget and not args.display:
        send("screen-role-forget"); print("monitor roles forgotten: roles follow left-to-right order")
        return
    if not args.display or (not args.role and not args.forget):
        die("screen-role needs DISPLAY ROLE (or DISPLAY --forget, or --forget)")
    status = fresh_status()
    externals = [sc for sc in status["screens"] if not sc["builtin"]]
    text = args.display.lower()
    hits = [sc for sc in externals if sc["id"] == text] or \
           [sc for sc in externals if sc.get("uuid", "").lower().startswith(text) and len(text) >= 4] or \
           [sc for sc in externals if text in sc["name"].lower()]
    if len(hits) != 1:
        die(f"'{args.display}' matches {len(hits)} connected monitors: "
            + ", ".join(f"{sc['id']} ({sc['name']}, {sc.get('uuid', '')[:8]})" for sc in externals))
    if args.forget:
        s = send(f"screen-role-forget/{hits[0]['uuid']}")
        print(f"{hits[0]['name']} forgotten: its role waits for a choice, its layout is not applied")
        return
    role = role_name(args.role)
    s = send(f"screen-role/{hits[0]['uuid']}/{role}")
    for sc in s["screens"]:
        if not sc["builtin"]:
            print(f"{sc['id']:<11} {sc['name']:<28} {sc.get('uuid', '')[:8]}")


def main():
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="deskmap", description=__doc__,
                                formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
    for name, fn in (("status", show_status), ("screens", show_screens), ("rules", show_rules)):
        sp = sub.add_parser(name); sp.add_argument("--json", action="store_true"); sp.set_defaults(fn=fn)
    sp = sub.add_parser("windows"); sp.add_argument("--app"); sp.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    sp.set_defaults(fn=show_windows)
    sub.add_parser("hooks").set_defaults(fn=show_hooks)
    sp = sub.add_parser("screen-role", help="give a connected monitor an external role; it keeps it")
    sp.add_argument("display", nargs="?"); sp.add_argument("role", nargs="?")
    sp.add_argument("--forget", action="store_true"); sp.set_defaults(fn=screen_role)
    for name in ("pause", "resume", "toggle", "reapply", "reload", "next-profile"):
        sub.add_parser(name).set_defaults(fn=lambda a, n=name: send(n))
    sp = sub.add_parser("profile"); sp.add_argument("name")
    sp.set_defaults(fn=lambda a: send("profile", name=a.name))
    for name in ("pin", "move"):
        sp = sub.add_parser(name); sp.add_argument("window"); sp.add_argument("screen")
        sp.add_argument("desktop", nargs="?", type=int); sp.set_defaults(fn=window_command(name))
        if name == "pin":
            sp.add_argument("--desktop-only", action="store_true",
                            help="follow the desktop only; keep the window's position and size")
    sp = sub.add_parser("unpin"); sp.add_argument("window"); sp.set_defaults(fn=window_command("unpin"))
    sp = sub.add_parser("free", help="let a pinned window move freely: 15m, 2h, lock (until the screen locks) or end")
    sp.add_argument("window"); sp.add_argument("duration"); sp.set_defaults(fn=free_move)
    sp = sub.add_parser("desktops"); sp.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    sp.set_defaults(fn=show_desktops)
    sp = sub.add_parser("name"); sp.add_argument("screen"); sp.add_argument("desktop", type=int)
    sp.add_argument("name", nargs="*"); sp.add_argument("--mode", choices=MODES)
    sp.set_defaults(fn=name_desktop)
    rp = sub.add_parser("rule").add_subparsers(dest="rcmd", required=True)
    sp = rp.add_parser("add")
    sp.add_argument("--app", required=True); sp.add_argument("--bundle")
    sp.add_argument("--title", nargs="+"); sp.add_argument("--screen")
    sp.add_argument("--desktop", type=int); sp.add_argument("--layout")
    sp.add_argument("--undocked-screen"); sp.add_argument("--undocked-desktop", type=int)
    sp.set_defaults(fn=rule_add)
    sp = rp.add_parser("rm"); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.set_defaults(fn=rule_rm)
    sp = sub.add_parser("profile-rename"); sp.add_argument("old"); sp.add_argument("new")
    sp.set_defaults(fn=lambda a: send(f"profile-rename/{urllib.parse.quote(a.old, safe='')}", name=a.new))
    sp = sub.add_parser("export"); sp.add_argument("file"); sp.add_argument("--profile")
    sp.set_defaults(fn=export_profile)
    sp = sub.add_parser("desktop-move"); sp.add_argument("screen"); sp.add_argument("src", type=int)
    sp.add_argument("dst", type=int); sp.add_argument("--mode", choices=MODES); sp.set_defaults(fn=desktop_move)
    sp = sub.add_parser("backups"); sp.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    sp.set_defaults(fn=show_backups)
    sub.add_parser("backup-now").set_defaults(fn=lambda a: (send("backup-now"), print("backed up")))
    sp = sub.add_parser("backup-restore"); sp.add_argument("id"); sp.set_defaults(fn=backup_restore)
    sp = sub.add_parser("save-layout"); sp.add_argument("rule"); sp.add_argument("--window")
    sp.set_defaults(fn=save_layout)
    sp = sub.add_parser("apply"); sp.add_argument("file", nargs="?")
    sp.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true"); sp.add_argument("--undo", action="store_true")
    sp.add_argument("--remove", action="store_true", help="remove the file's rules from the profile")
    sp.add_argument("--wait", type=float, default=8.0, help="seconds to wait for launched apps")
    sp.set_defaults(fn=lambda a: apply_layout(a) if a.undo or a.file else die("apply needs a file or --undo"))
    sp = sub.add_parser("check"); sp.add_argument("file"); sp.set_defaults(fn=check_layout)
    sp = sub.add_parser("dump"); sp.add_argument("--docked", nargs="+"); sp.add_argument("--undocked", nargs="+")
    sp.add_argument("--title", nargs="+"); sp.add_argument("-o", "--output"); sp.set_defaults(fn=dump_layout)
    sub.add_parser("layouts").set_defaults(fn=lambda a: print("\n".join(
        f"{k:<18} {','.join(f'{v:g}' for v in xywh)}" for k, xywh in NAMED_LAYOUTS.items())
        + "\ndesktop-only       follow the desktop, keep position and size"))
    if len(sys.argv) == 1:
        p.print_help()
        return
    args = p.parse_args()
    args.fn(args)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
